# spark-project-model Rules

These rules apply to `packages/spark-project-model/`.

## Model Direction

**Design is editing** — do not split "design layer" vs "edit layer" in docs or naming.

`ProjectModel` is the class hierarchy root (design + runtime). `ProjectEditor` is the **design facade** (API + `EditorSession` + `subscribe` + persistence), not a competing domain.

```text
ProjectModel.design.navigation  # NavigationDesign owns nodesById
ProjectModel.design             # config pages Map
ProjectEditor                   # thin orchestrator + collaborators
```

## Source Layout

```text
model/project|navigation|page|serialization/
facade/        project-editor, editor-session, *-editor collaborators
factory/       page-node-factory
io/            file, navigation, loader, reference, http
index.ts       model public API
project.ts     facade + artifact public API
```

Dependency: `facade → {model, io}`, `io → model`, `factory → {model, io}`. **Never `model → io`.** DevSystem designer artifacts live in app `src/services/project-model-artifacts/`. Distinguish **model (types)** in package vs **domain instance** (`editor.project`) vs **facade instance** (`getAppProjectEditor()` in APP). Do not call `ProjectEditor` the "model instance". DevSystem Vue calls `state.editor` (facade) — no parallel file layer.

Maps: `src/STRUCTURE.md`, `src/MODEL-HIERARCHY.md`.

## Boundaries

- Persistent truth: DB navigation + page files only.
- In-memory model shape need not mirror storage; save must map to `nodeId` / `pageId` / file anchors.
- Session state (`selected`, `dirty`, working DTO) lives in `EditorSession`, not `ProjectModel`.
- No Vue/DOM/Router/Element Plus in this package.
- Fail fast on missing APIs, invalid config, unloaded pages.

## Public Surface

```text
@spark-appworks/spark-project-model
@spark-appworks/spark-project-model/project
```

No cross-package `src/*` deep imports.

